.TH CMX 1 2026-10-17 "cmx 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.\" Left-aligned and unhyphenated, so key names and paths copy as written.
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
cmx \- cmx, a starting point for GTK 4 apps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmx
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmx
opens a window that shows a greeting.
It runs as a single instance: when it is already running, the new window opens in
that process.
.PP
Every window has the Wayland app_id
.BR io.github.DisposableSoftware.cmx ,
so compositor window rules can match it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Neither option opens a window or contacts a running cmx.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Each binding has a name, used in the
.B [keybindings]
group of
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmx/keybindings.ini
(see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
To change one, write the name and a list of GTK accelerators separated by
.BR ; ,
for example
.BR "quit = <Ctrl>q;<Alt>F4" .
An empty value unbinds it.
.TP
.B new\-window
New window.
Opens another window.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>n\fR
.TP
.B close\-window
Close window.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>w\fR
.TP
.B quit
Quit.
Closes every window.
.br
Keys: \fB<Ctrl>q\fR
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmx/config.ini
(usually
.IR ~/.config/cmx/config.ini )
when cmx starts; restart it to apply changes.
The file uses GLib key-file (INI) syntax and every key is optional.
.PP
When
.I config.ini
or
.I keybindings.ini
is missing, cmx creates it on start, listing every setting or binding at
its default but commented out: remove the leading
.B #
from a line and edit it.
A file that already exists is never written to, even when it is a symlink.
The same examples, with the values live, are installed as
.I share/doc/cmx/config.example.ini
and
.IR share/doc/cmx/keybindings.example.ini .
.SS [window]
.TP
.B width
The default window width in logical pixels, 300 to 8192.
.br
Default: \fB800\fR
.TP
.B height
The default window height in logical pixels, 200 to 8192.
.br
Default: \fB600\fR
.SS [view]
.TP
.B greeting
The text shown in the window.
.br
Default: \fBHello\fR
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmx/config.ini
Settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cmx/keybindings.ini
Key bindings.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the settings are read; default
.IR ~/.config .
